; Collinear leading creases cannot pick a stayer side. A legal 4-ray vertex
; (the two square diagonals crossing at the centre — a waterbomb-style vertex,
; Maekawa 3V/1M) whose leading pair is the two OPPOSITE rays of a single
; diagonal (--d1 toward .a and toward .c). Their folded rays are collinear, so
; the <180 arc between them is undefined and the convention has no side to
; anchor. Without (staying <flap>) this must error, pointing the user at the
; clause that would resolve it.

paper square

mark --d1 = through .a .c
mark --d2 = through .b .d

flatten (--d1 & .a) (--d1 & .c) (--d2 & .b mountain) (--d2 & .d)

; expect error "collinear leading creases"
